    "objective": "Audit and visually polish the current UI.\n\nDo not immediately start rewriting components.\n\nFirst inspect the actual implementation, including the relevant MDUI components, custom CSS, layout structure, and assistant-ui integration.\n\nThen:\n\n1. Identify the 5–10 most important visual problems.\n   Focus on:\n\n   * hierarchy and scan path,\n   * spacing rhythm,\n   * typography,\n   * alignment,\n   * information density,\n   * color hierarchy,\n   * surfaces / borders / elevation,\n   * interaction states,\n   * visual consistency between the task UI and assistant-ui,\n   * responsive behavior.\n\n2. Identify any obvious AI-generated UI patterns:\n\n   * unnecessary cards,\n   * nested containers,\n   * excessive rounded rectangles,\n   * excessive whitespace,\n   * generic dashboard composition,\n   * decorative gradients or glow,\n   * inconsistent iconography,\n   * weak visual hierarchy,\n   * repeated spacing values with no grouping logic.\n\n3. Define one restrained visual direction for this screen in 2–4 words.\n\n4. Propose the smallest high-impact set of changes.\n\n5. Implement those changes using the existing architecture.\n\nConstraints:\n\n* Keep MDUI as the primary design system.\n* Prefer MDUI design tokens/CSS variables over hard-coded visual values.\n* Preserve assistant-ui behavior and architecture.\n* Do not introduce another UI framework.\n* Do not rewrite working application logic for visual reasons.\n* Do not make this look like a landing page.\n* Do not add decorative elements unless they improve hierarchy, affordance, or comprehension.\n\nAfter implementation, review the result again as a product designer.\n\nSpecifically check whether removing any newly added container, border, background, radius, shadow, badge, or animation would make the interface cleaner without reducing comprehension. If yes, remove it.\n\nThe final result should feel intentional, quiet, polished, cohesive, and optimized for repeated daily use rather than visually impressive in a screenshot.",
